; The zone this cloud answers for. $ORIGIN is the zone's own fqdn and is
; supplied by the platform, so this file does not repeat it -- which is what
; lets the same file serve a zone that gets renamed.
;
; EVERYTHING A ZONE FILE HAS IS USABLE HERE, and that is the point of it being
; a file: `@` for the apex, a TTL that defaults per-record, a comment that
; explains a record to whoever reads it next, and parentheses to carry one
; record across lines. None of that survived a list of strings in yaml.

@       3600    IN  MX      10 mail.example.com.

; SPF, split across lines the way a long TXT is written by hand.
@       3600    IN  TXT     ( "v=spf1"
                              "include:_spf.google.com"
                              "~all" )

docs     300    IN  CNAME   hosted.notion.so.
vpn      300    IN  A       203.0.113.9
